# LeakSanitizer suppressions for HardScript v0.1.1 audit.
#
# These are intentionally process-lifetime singletons: function-local static
# registries that are cheap to construct once and never individually freed.
# They are not per-request or per-connection allocations, so they are not
# memory-safety bugs. Everything else must be leak-free.
leak:hs::ws_registry
leak:hs::ws_clients
leak:hs::ws_rooms
leak:hs::ws_client_room
leak:hs::test_registry